This is an audit-readable overlay specification. Exact executable authority is:
`tooling/llm-api-bridges/ozon-seller/validation/materialize_patch_a3_refresh_response_boundary_candidate.py`

Confirmed A.2 browser failure:
- `OZ_WORK_REFRESH` returned ok=true and advertised runtime reload;
- after 30 seconds the service-worker target ID was still exactly the old target ID;
- no new runtime generation and no `WORK_SESSION_REFRESH_RESUMED` appeared;
- therefore the old-worker `setTimeout(() => chrome.runtime.reload(), 0)` did not provide a reliable MV3 message-event-lifetime boundary.

Patch A.3 changes only `service_worker.js` and preserves all A.1/A.2 durable recovery, provider, quota, cache, history and no-replay semantics.

Production changes:

1. REMOVE pre-runtime page reload from the old worker.

The A.2 route no longer calls `chrome.tabs.reload(tab)` before extension runtime reload. A content script loaded from the old extension runtime would be invalidated by the following extension reload and is not a reliable recovery bootstrap.

2. REMOVE timer-dependent runtime reload.

The A.2 route no longer executes:

`setTimeout(() => chrome.runtime.reload(), 0);`

Instead the route returns an internal, non-public marker:

`runtime_reload_after_response: true`

alongside public fields:

- `ok=true`
- recovery
- `runtime_reload_scheduled=true`
- `page_reload_deferred_to_new_runtime=true`
- `wake_alarm_scheduled`

The route records:

`WORK_SESSION_REFRESH_RUNTIME_RELOAD_ARMED`

before returning.

3. RELOAD EXTENSION AT THE MESSAGE RESPONSE BOUNDARY.

The common `chrome.runtime.onMessage` promise completion handler checks the internal marker.

For ordinary messages behavior is unchanged: `sendResponse(response)`.

For Refresh only:

- clone response;
- remove the internal marker;
- call `sendResponse(publicResponse)` first;
- immediately, in the same active message callback/microtask turn, call `chrome.runtime.reload()` directly;
- no timer, interval or later callback is required from the old worker.

This preserves a public successful Refresh acknowledgment while guaranteeing that runtime reload is invoked before the old MV3 message event can become idle.

4. NEW RUNTIME OWNS THE PAGE RELOAD.

Add:

`reloadRefreshOwnerTabAfterRuntimeRenewal(recovery)`

The new service-worker generation, during durable recovery resume, calls `chrome.tabs.reload(recovery.tab_id)` itself before waiting for `OZ_GET_IDENTITY`.

On success it records:

`WORK_SESSION_REFRESH_POST_RUNTIME_TAB_RELOAD_SCHEDULED`

with the new `WORKER_SESSION_ID`.

Then the existing A.2 bounded reconnect loop waits for the fresh manifest content script created by that new-runtime page reload.

5. POST-RUNTIME TAB RELOAD FAILS CLOSED.

If the new runtime cannot reload the exact owner tab:

- command acceptance stays false;
- matching `recovering` session becomes `error`;
- matching durable recovery is removed;
- diagnostic `WORK_REFRESH_TAB_RELOAD_FAILED` is recorded with new runtime generation;
- no provider request/replay occurs.

6. EXISTING A.2 recovery semantics remain:

- durable recovery intent and operation terminalization;
- one-shot wake alarm fallback;
- single-flight resume;
- 15-second / 250-ms fresh content-runtime reconnect wait;
- exact tab/origin/adapter/conversation correlation;
- `OZ_WORK_RUNTIME_RENEW` generation handshake;
- restore `active_visible` or `active_hidden`;
- visible-only command acceptance restore;
- hidden recovery remains hidden until explicit Show;
- `WORK_SESSION_REFRESH_RESUMED` old/new generation diagnostic;
- protected provider quota/cache/history/no-replay state preserved.

No other production file changes.
